{"id": "tea:samten-ngalso:ch1", "source": "src:samten-ngalso", "location": {"ref": "ch1"}, "paraphrase": "The place for meditation: a solitary, pleasant place suited to the season and to one's practice — high and open for clarity, enclosed for calm — free of dangers and disturbances.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["meditation"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["practice"], "teachers": ["tch:longchenpa"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "translation_basis": "Tibetan (paraphrase by the unit)", "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U45-nyingma-bon"], "disagreements": []}, "notes": "Reference from the unit author's knowledge (not read in a local text in this phase).", "coverage": ["B6", "D"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U45-nyingma-bon"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:samten-ngalso:ch2", "source": "src:samten-ngalso", "location": {"ref": "ch2"}, "paraphrase": "The person who meditates: one with renunciation, faith and diligence, who has turned from worldly concerns, keeps the vows and relies on a qualified teacher.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["meditation"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["practice", "teacher-transmission"], "teachers": ["tch:longchenpa"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "translation_basis": "Tibetan (paraphrase by the unit)", "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U45-nyingma-bon"], "disagreements": []}, "notes": "Reference from the unit author's knowledge (not read in a local text in this phase).", "coverage": ["B6", "D"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U45-nyingma-bon"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:samten-ngalso:ch3", "source": "src:samten-ngalso", "location": {"ref": "ch3"}, "paraphrase": "The practice: preliminaries, then the main meditations that bring the experiences of bliss, clarity and non-thought, each to be released without attachment lest it lead into the desire, form or formless realms; then non-conceptual wisdom.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["practice", "powers-experiences"], "concepts": ["cpt:nyams-bliss-clarity-nonthought"], "obstacles": ["obs:attachment-to-nyams"], "teachers": ["tch:longchenpa"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "translation_basis": "Tibetan (paraphrase by the unit)", "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U45-nyingma-bon"], "disagreements": []}, "notes": "Reference from the unit author's knowledge (not read in a local text in this phase).", "coverage": ["B6", "D"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U45-nyingma-bon"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
